00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.520
Onii-chan.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.910
Do you believe in things like ghosts?

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:48.850
Ghosts?

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.430
What about them?

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.290
Did you hear something from Sengoku?

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.780
Why is Nadeko-chan's name coming up?

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.910
Onii-chan, sometimes you talk nonsense.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.660
Oh, it's nothing.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.500
But why are you talking about ghosts all of a sudden?

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.120
What is it?

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.930
Is there a ghost in the Tea Ceremony Club room?

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.170
That's it exactly. How did you know?

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:11.190
<b>LUCKY GUESS</b>

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.920
To be precise, it's a story about how a ghost
used to appear in the Tea Ceremony Club room.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.350
"Used to appear"?

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.530
What do you mean?

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.960
Were there any traces left behind
in the Tea Ceremony Club room?

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.430
No, it's hard to tell if any traces were left behind.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:32.190
There's no objective proof that such a girl was there.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.080
"Such a girl"?

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.570
<b>THAT'S RATHER SPECIFIC.</b>

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.010
Tsukihi, let me tell you some good news.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.840
The fact that there's no evidence
means there wasn't a ghost.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.090
Okay! That ends this conversation.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.300
Now we can spend the rest of the time in idle chatter.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.720
Toh!

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.500
What I want is to consult.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.230
It's definitely not just idle chatter.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.890
Okay, I get it.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.070
There, there.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.220
I get it, so put that ballpoint pen away.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.120
Put it away?

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.320
What color of this three-color
ballpoint pen should I put away?

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.410
All of them.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.060
Red, blue, and black, all three.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.060
Wait. What did you mean by that?

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.640
You said that there used to be a ghost
in the Tea Ceremony Club room,

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.830
but there's no evidence?

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.340
That's what I've been telling you.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.580
Weren't you listening?

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:21.360
I'm guessing you proved there weren't any ghosts, didn't you?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.630
Wow, how did you figure that out?{insert crash-bandicoot-woah.mp3}

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.120
<i>I'm pretty sure this is what happened.</i>

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.620
<i>Rumors were spreading about a ghost
in the Tea Ceremony Club room.</i>

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:34.140
<i>Tsukihi, not as part of the Fire Sisters,</i>

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.270
<i>but independently as Tsukihi Araragi, plunged into the investigation.</i>

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.260
<i>And she solved the mystery.</i>

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.740
What do you think I should do, Onii-chan?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.010
About what?

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.640
Well, I mean...

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:51.930
I orderly and logically explained to them that the ghost doesn't exist,

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.190
but none of them believe me.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:58.480
They believe in the ghost more than they believe me.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.090
There are seven members in the Tea Ceremony Club.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.950
The rumor is that there's an eighth member,
so I addressed each source of it,

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.480
like eyewitness accounts and circumstantial evidence,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.580
and logically disproved each of them.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.080
Logically.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.580
Don't stress "logically" so much.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.770
It makes it sound like a lie.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.520
Like a lie? How rude!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:24.880
I went through quite the ordeal to refute the existence of the "eighth member."

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.410
But everyone replied to me like,

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.160
"That may be how it is, but, well..."

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.270
"What you're saying may be correct,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.650
it may be how it is logically,

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.040
but even then, the 'eighth member' may have been here."

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.270
...and so on!

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.050
The rumors won't go away at all!

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.230
What do you think, Onii-chan?

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.760
What do you think I should do?

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.120
What should you do?

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.830
What do you think is a good way to go about this?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.770
How do I put it?{in}

00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:00.840
I'm asserting what's correct,
and people understand that it is,

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:06.220
so things like opposition and battling with opinions are done.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:10.490
But the original situation hasn't changed at all, I guess?

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.840
What's "correct" is meaningless.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.730
It had no effect at all.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.480
What should I do about that?

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:19.420
They didn't counter your argument,
but rather, they all ignored it,

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:24.630
and even now, everyone's still going on
about the "eighth member"?

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.130
That's right.{ZATSU RAITO}

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:30.370
<b>FOR THIS CASE,</b>

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:30.410
<b>FOR THIS CASE,</b>

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:30.450
<b>FOR THIS CASE,</b>

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:30.490
<b>FOR THIS CASE,</b>

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:30.580
<b>HOW SHOULD I GO ABOUT GIVING HER ADVICE?</b>

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:30.620
<b>HOW SHOULD I GO ABOUT GIVING HER ADVICE?</b>

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:30.660
<b>HOW SHOULD I GO ABOUT GIVING HER ADVICE?</b>

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.760
<b>HOW SHOULD I GO ABOUT GIVING HER ADVICE?</b>

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.490
Hey, Tsukihi-chan.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.100
What is it you want me to do?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.690
Why are you asking that?

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.600
Onii-chan, weren't you listening to my story?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.000
Well, you have a shocked look on your face, but...

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.690
Even with that reprimanding tone of voice
and a shocked look on your face...

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:49.570
Tei!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.830
<b>MY SKIN NARROWLY ESCAPED BEING MARKED BY THREE COLORS.</b>

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.170
Be blunt, Tsukihi-chan.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.490
What exactly do you want me to do?

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.280
I'm troubled that you're asking "what."

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.410
No, well, I want to ask your opinion.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.090
I want to do some research.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.590
Onii-chan, do you believe in things like ghosts?

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.050
<b>WE'RE BACK TO THE FIRST QUESTION.</b>

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.600
What?

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.040
Why do you look so troubled trying to answer, Onii-chan?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.830
This is a simple yes or no answer, right?

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.180
No, Tsukihi-chan.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:23.170
Problems in the world don't always have a simple yes or no answer.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.310
Is that so?

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:28.420
I mean, your existence can be a yes or no answer.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.450
No.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.680
I don't believe in ghosts.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.190
The other Tea Ceremony Club members are all mistaken.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:40.200
I guarantee you're correct, so don't worry about it.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.190
You should stay true to yourself
and push forward with your correctness.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.940
You're right.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.160
But it's still on my mind.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.170
Well, whether you acknowledge or deny
the "eighth member's" existence,

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.080
or whether it gets acknowledged or denied,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.220
the situation isn't so severe that the Tea Ceremony Club will disband.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.710
It's just that she's hit a wall.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:03.850
A wall?

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.350
For Tsukihi-chan, a hero of justice,

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:11.130
it must be uncomfortable to be in an environment
where what's correct is being ignored.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:16.930
A situation where the absurd and illogical
have more influence, and for no reason,

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.240
probably happens often in real life.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:23.480
Having such an irrational experience
will benefit her in the future.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.100
Irrational, huh?

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.200
I think it's rational enough.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:31.760
So, I feel like I want to side with Tsukihi-chan.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:35.240
You always side with the cute girls.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.490
No, how cute they are doesn't matter in this case.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:43.460
If so, it could be that the other six members
of the Tea Ceremony Club are cute, too.

